d a total cost of ",{"type":"span","props":{"id":"mwIg"},"children":[{"type":"span","props":{},"children":[{"type":"span","props":{},"children":["Cash"]}]},"$61,500"]},"."]},"\n\n"]},{"type":"section","props":{"id":"mwIw"},"children":[{"type":"h2","props":{"id":"Appearance"},"children":["Appearance"]},"\n",{"type":"p","props":{},"children":["There were three different types of ",{"type":"b","props":{},"children":["Super Computer Parts"]},", each with a different appearance. The first type of part resembled a server, with a long, flat body with ports at each end to power and connect the server to the mainframe. The second type of part resembled a miniature display setup, with a bolted panel and a small screen that functioned as a display. The third type of part resembled an antenna, with two thin rods bolted into a receiver that was attached to the side of the Super Computer. "]},"\n\n"]},{"type":"section","props":{"id":"mwJg"},"children":[{"type":"h2","props":{"id":"Strategy"},"children":["Strategy"]},"\n",{"type":"ul","props":{},"children":[{"type":"li","props":{},"children":["Because the ",{"type":"b","props":{},"children":["Super Computer Parts"]}," can be bought on any wave before the final wave, it is best to reserve buying them all until Wave 18 or 19, where cash is more abundant. \n",{"type":"ul","props":{},"children":[{"type":"li","props":{},"children":[{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/Dispatcher","title":"Dispatcher"},"children":["Dispatcher"]}," will remind the players to buy parts, though this does not mean they have to be bought."]}]}]}]},"\n\n"]},{"type":"section","props":{"id":"mwLQ"},"children":[{"type":"h2","props":{"id":"Trivia"},"children":["Trivia"]},"\n",{"type":"ul","props":{},"children":[{"type":"li","props":{},"children":[{"type":"a","props":{"href":"https://www.roblox.com/users/31164652/profile#!/about"},"children":["Enthrallist"]}," created the sound effects for the ",{"type":"b","props":{},"children":["Super Computer"]}," using an electromag